WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:06.100
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, a lot of you
requested an Arrow video so this is going

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.120
to be all about the new Heroes of the second
half of the season.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.559
Power abhors a vacuum.

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:13.219
So let’s start with a question?

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:16.510
What happens when your main hero vacates his
role?

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.860
One or more characters step in to fill it.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.160
So the second half of the season is going
to kind of spin the Joseph Campbell archetype

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:29.760
wheel on everyone.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:38.149
Bad Guys will be heroes, and new bad guys
will step in to fill that void too.

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:42.430
It’s way more complicated than that.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:47.399
But what I’m suggesting is that Merlyn and
the other Team Arrow members are the heroes

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:51.659
while Oliver is away and in present day, we’ll
be following their journey.

00:00:51.659 --> 00:00:56.100
We will still follow Oliver’s journey in
flashbacks but this video is mostly about

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.780
what’s going on in present day.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:03.389
In case you’re not familiar with that, Joseph
Campbell wrote a book about the different

00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:11.160
archetypes characters represent to each other
at various points in a story.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:15.800
Careful for spoilers through Episode 9, I
have to reference some specific details.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.710
Rewind to Season 1.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:22.690
Just taking the show at face value, Oliver
is the protagonist.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:27.150
The story is about his journey to becoming
the Justice League super hero Green Arrow.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.800
Malcolm Merlyn is the main villain.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.980
Oliver has to defeat Darth Merlyn before he
can call himself a Jedi.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.540
Oh wait, wrong franchise.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.380
Isn’t it crazy to think about through the
star wars lens though.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:41.560
In that scenario, Oliver would have to ultimately
redeem Merlyn.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:02:04.670
So that’s something to file away under the
maybe pile in your mind palace.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:08.750
So pushing deeper into the Lazarus Pit here,
when you look at the story from the different

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.460
viewpoints of each of the characters.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:15.480
Everyone’s role, or their archetype changes
depending on which character you’re thinking

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.480
about.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.680
Malcolm Merlyn for instance, is always going
to be the Hero of his own story.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.510
If you were John Barrowman and someone asked
you who the hero of the show was.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.510
You’d say Malcolm Merlyn.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:23.510
Grain of salt, maybe he goes a little overboard
sometimes.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.710
Like drugging his daughter’s tea to get
her older brother to help you out of your

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.110
jam with your former boss.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:29.350
But you’re not a bad guy, you just want
your family back.

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.640
Forget those lazer eyes Oliver is shooting
at you.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:35.510
Seriously, every time oliver makes this face
at Merlyn, I picture him boring a hole in

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:37.819
the back of Merlyn’s skull with Superman
heat vision.

00:02:37.819 --> 00:02:41.300
Oliver is, by all accounts, dead when things
pick up in Episode 10.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:46.530
At least he’s dead to the world, even if
he’s not Capital “D” dead as in “The

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:47.530
Final Death”.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:55.280
His role in the story needs to be filled by
another character or multiple characters.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:00.450
Appropriately, the title of Episode 10 is
“Left Behind”.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:06.819
It largely refers to Team Arrow Proper, but
now that Oliver is gone and only Merlyn knows

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:12.040
what’s really going on, I think he’ll
integrate himself into Team Arrow, a little.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.290
Let’s remember that Felicity and Diggle
are nobody’s fool, she’s not going to

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.290
trust Merlyn.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.630
And as gullible as Roy looks, he’ll listen
to Felicity and Diggle.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:25.319
Laurel, Ted Grant and Ray Palmer are also
waiting in the wings to help when called upon.

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:27.840
Thea is kind of an X factor in all this, yes.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.930
I think she’ll also be one of the heroes
but both she and Merlyn also have this Loki

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.280
Trickster thing going on.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:39.810
In Joseph Cambell’s book there are The Hero,
the mentor, the guardian of the threshold,

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:48.830
the herald, the shapeshifter, the shadow and
the trickster.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:54.180
All of the character represent different things
to each other.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:04:00.069
For the most part the different archetypes
Team Arrow embody are all positive.

00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:03.640
Sometimes characters will change their roles
in each new scene.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:06.060
But just looking at the next block of episodes
in general.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.060
Like the next 5 episodes.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.819
Merlyn will be one of the biggest new heroes.

00:04:08.819 --> 00:04:09.950
Mostly from his own perspective.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.209
But he’ll be a much bigger presence on the
show.

00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:13.790
Not to forget Laurel becoming Black Canary.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.410
We should just say that she’s going to be
wearing the costume, but calling her Black

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:19.720
Canary right away is like calling Oliver Green
Arrow.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.299
He’s not Green Arrow yet.

00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:24.380
So let’s just continue to think of her as
a stabby Laurel.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.380
What about Oliver though?

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:26.860
When is he coming back in present day.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:28.080
How is he coming back?

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.700
In case you haven’t read it, these are the
steps in what Joseph Campbell called the Hero’s

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:31.700
journey.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:32.700
1.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:33.700
Heroes are introduced in the ORDINARY WORLD,
where

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:34.700
1.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:35.700
they receive the CALL TO ADVENTURE.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:36.700
1.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:37.700
They are RELUCTANT at first or REFUSE THE
CALL, but

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:38.700
1.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:39.700
are encouraged by a MENTOR to

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:40.700
1.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:41.700
CROSS THE FIRST THRESHOLD and enter the Special
World, where

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:42.700
1.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.700
they encounter TESTS, ALLIES, AND ENEMIES.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:44.700
1.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.171
They APPROACH THE INMOST CAVE, crossing a
second threshold

00:04:46.171 --> 00:04:47.171
2.

00:04:47.171 --> 00:04:50.120
where they endure the ORDEAL.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.120
1.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.790
They take possession of their REWARD and

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:53.790
1.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:06:38.479
are pursued on 

00:06:38.479 --> 00:06:43.260
THE ROAD BACK to the Ordinary World.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.260
1.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:48.100
They cross the third threshold, experience
a RESURRECTION, and are transformed by the

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.100
experience.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:50.100
1.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:59.880
They RETURN WITH THE ELIXIR, a boon or treasure
to benefit the Ordinary World.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:04.270
Marc Guggenheim and the other Arrow writers
don’t completely stick to the Joseph Campbell

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:07.080
storyline, but there are a lot of similarities.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:11.440
Really I think most of our questions about
the characters in the second half are first,

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:13.920
what is the mechanism by which Oliver comes
back.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:17.840
And two, when are we going to see the big
super hero justice society team up?

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:24.199
A lot of you have been pointing to the fan
art of the Lazarus Pit and yes Marc Guggenhiem

00:07:24.199 --> 00:07:27.889
has said he’s reversed his decision to not
do superpowers on Arrow.

00:07:27.889 --> 00:07:32.750
But I think the Lazarus Pit on Arrow will
be something much more practical.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:35.870
They’ll still play it as realistic as possible.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:39.009
They just did Mirakuru in Season 2.

00:07:39.009 --> 00:07:43.479
I think they’re not going to go miracle
cure route.

00:07:43.479 --> 00:07:53.220
But I do think someone tied to the League
will heal Oliver using their methods.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:58.990
Malcolm Merlyn said that Nanda Parbat was
a place where death doesn’t mean anything

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:03.080
and The title of Episode 15 this year is Nanda
Parbat.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:04.880
Even if Oliver doesn’t come back in that
episode.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.880
I think we’ll find out how he’s going
to come back.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:11.729
For those that are wondering Episode 14 is
called The Return.

00:08:11.729 --> 00:08:14.700
That refers to Tommy coming back.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:18.810
Colin O’Donnell filmed scenes, probably
in flashback just like when he appeared at

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:21.800
the beginning of the season in Hong Kong.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:26.110
Stephen Amell posted this picture to facebook
saying, “We wouldn’t shoot our 60th episode

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:42.390
of Arrow without Colin O’Donnell”.

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:51.640
So “The Return” has nothing to do with
Oliver returning.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:55.860
Yes, Manu Bennett is appearing in it.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:09:04.370
But the title is a reference to Tommy, not
Deathstroke.

